  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000118932,
      "SummaryText": "Kinder Morgan Santa Fe Pacific Pipeline, LLC - Reno Terminal is a bulk petroleum storage and distribution facility that includes butane blending operations. This Risk Management Plan (RMP) covers the Butane Blending process including the associated piping and two 65,000 gallon butane storage vessels.  Kinder Morgan owns the real property associated with the Butane Blending process. Energy Transfer owns all the equipment associated with the Butane Blending process.  Energy Transfer and Kinder Morgan each have operational responsibilities for the Butane Blending process.   Energy Transfer controls and monitors all butane blending operations remotely from its control center located near Houston, Texas, conducts all maintenance activities, and schedules the delivery of butane trucks.  Kinder Morgan oversees the unloading of butane trucks into the storage vessels, and conducts routine visual inspections.\n\nEnergy Transfer constructed the Butane Blending process in accordance with the National Fire Protection Association (NFPA Code) No. 58 (2020 Edition) for Liquefied Petroleum Gas Storage. Energy Transfer designed, constructed, and maintains the Butane Blending process, in accordance with NFPA No. 58 and the manufacturer's instructions and recommendations. It is the Parties' policy to adhere to all applicable federal, state, and local laws/codes. \n\nThis facility has not had an accident involving butane which has resulted in deaths, injuries, property/environmental damage, evacuations, or sheltering in place.\n\nIn the event of an emergency involving the Butane Blending process, it is the Parties' policy to initially contact the owner of the equipment, Energy Transfer and the local fire department. The facility emergency response plans are coordinated with the local fire department and local emergency responders were invited to attend an initial training session for this system.\n\nProcess safety controls include excess flow valves, low-melting point pneumatic valve feeds to p"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000118932,
      "SummaryText": "neumatic valves (fail closed), 85% fill shut-off (90% ESD actuation) on the vessels, emergency shut-off devices on the system and video display terminal, line thermal/hydrostatic reliefs, and grounding interlock devices. Note: In contrast to the PSM requirements, this \"stationary source\" as defined under 40 CFR Part 68 is bounded by the off-load station and the points of injection.\n\nThe Parties actively seek employee input on process safety improvements. Additionally, local emergency responders are contacted periodically regarding participation in site emergency response drills."
    }
  ]
